WEBVTT

00:00:01.370 --> 00:00:04.480
<i>I just kept killing, and this is how I ended up.</i>

00:00:04.810 --> 00:00:06.910
<i>Killing? Killing what?</i>

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:08.360
<i>People...</i>

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:09.210
<i>Right?</i>

00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:11.570
<i>The Killer of 99, Koikawa Shungiku.</i>

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:38.730
Tsukishima, it isn't happening...

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:42.030
As it is, I'm amazed you were able 
to get this rock all the way here.

00:01:42.330 --> 00:01:47.040
If I'm going to be fighting bugs, 
I've gotta be able to cut this!

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:55.170
<i>And also so Mugai-dono accepts me!</i>

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:03.640
The best thing for a hangover is more drink!

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:13.190
I got a nosebleed!

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:17.610
H-Hey!

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:23.520
That cut was so clean, it shines like a mirror!

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:25.450
His stance was perfect...

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:29.320
Even using a beat-up, old katana like that!

00:02:33.880 --> 00:02:37.380
Koikawa-dono, please train 
me in the art of the blade!

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:40.470
What's this about, new kid?

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:42.760
How can I learn to cut a rock that way?

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:44.330
A rock?

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:45.900
Oh, that...

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:47.760
Nothing to it.

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:49.700
Just approach it like a konjac yam.

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:50.460
What?

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:51.520
Konjac, you say?

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:58.280
Konjac is very hard.

00:02:59.230 --> 00:03:01.540
It isn't konjac, you stupid kid.

00:03:05.510 --> 00:03:08.540
<b>The Killer of 99, 
Koikawa Shungiku!</b>

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:12.750
See you later.

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:17.000
Murderer...

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:18.300
It's the Killer of 99, Shungiku.

00:03:26.420 --> 00:03:29.320
Why are you even alive?

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:34.100
You criminal!

00:03:38.060 --> 00:03:39.500
Stop it, kid.

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:45.660
It's only natural for them to 
want to throw rocks at me.

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:47.460
Got it?

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:51.460
Hang around me, and all of Edo
 will hate you, too.

00:03:51.990 --> 00:03:54.520
I am a murderer.

00:03:55.410 --> 00:03:56.440
No!

00:03:56.440 --> 00:04:00.630
Now that I've chosen you as my master, 
my duty is to follow you everywhere.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:22.790
Who are those guys?

00:04:23.390 --> 00:04:25.770
Arson and theft investigators.

00:04:25.770 --> 00:04:28.720
They're looking into those serial robberies.

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:29.990
Burglaries?

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:34.410
The houses of local merchants and 
of the rich have been robbed.

00:04:35.530 --> 00:04:38.040
What's interesting is how it's being pulled off.

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:41.340
They cut cleanly through walls or iron doors.

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:45.040
I'm impressed that you know this, Koikawa-dono.

00:04:46.100 --> 00:04:47.650
Well, I was the one who did it...

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:49.160
Wh-What?!

00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:53.250
That was a joke, kid.

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:55.020
I wouldn't steal.

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:56.230
However,

00:04:57.110 --> 00:04:58.980
I would kill.

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:05.160
Our patrol's done for the day.

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:07.570
I'm going to go drink alone.

00:05:07.570 --> 00:05:09.100
You do what you like.

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:11.250
Then I'll go with you—

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:12.580
Don't even think about it!

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:15.080
See you around, kid.

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:23.480
Oharu-dono, may I have some more?

00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:24.830
Sure!

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:25.840
Jinbei-sama,

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:27.500
order as much as you like.

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:31.670
That samurai eats a lot.

00:05:31.670 --> 00:05:34.580
We're out of the good rice.

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:36.690
Then go and get some more.

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:37.390
Huh?

00:05:37.890 --> 00:05:43.160
We need Jinbei-sama to 
keep fighting bugs for us.

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:48.900
You've become very close to him.

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:52.030
So, are you at the age when you fall in love?

00:05:52.390 --> 00:05:54.470
Oh, Grandpa!

00:05:54.180 --> 00:05:55.580
That's dangerous...

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:58.330
<b>Magistrates</b>

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:57.080
The magistrates are here!

00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:58.330
There was a robbery in Iseya!

00:05:58.770 --> 00:05:59.960
Wh-What?

00:06:12.410 --> 00:06:13.910
What are you looking at?

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:20.850
<b>Kodenma Prison</b>

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:21.450
Wait!

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:24.560
Please release Koikawa-dono!

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:26.520
What are you talking about?

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:30.110
You saw him at the crime scene, 
with a bloodstained katana.

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:34.330
But he hasn't admitted his guilt!

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:36.680
If he won't tell us why he was there,

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:38.370
then essentially, he has.

00:06:39.330 --> 00:06:42.080
But he didn't do it!

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:43.420
I believe in him!

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:48.640
Hey, is he serious?

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:51.140
How could he believe in a guy like that?

00:06:51.820 --> 00:06:55.050
I know you're new to the Insect Magistrate's Office,
but you should wake up.

00:06:55.050 --> 00:06:59.310
He's a criminal who's done 
many evil things in Edo.

00:06:59.660 --> 00:07:02.390
A murderer will always be a murderer!

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:06.820
Kotori-dono!

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:10.870
Use your authority to get 
Koikawa-dono out of prison!

00:07:10.870 --> 00:07:13.070
Tell them to release him!

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:15.680
He can't be released so quickly.

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:16.950
Wh-What?

00:07:17.480 --> 00:07:20.220
For one thing, we don't know

00:07:20.220 --> 00:07:23.820
why he refuses to tell us 
the reason he was there.

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:25.680
It's possible he did it.

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:26.670
Hibachi-dono!

00:07:27.190 --> 00:07:29.150
Even if we had him released,

00:07:29.150 --> 00:07:31.410
the Insect Magistrate is a bureaucracy, too.

00:07:31.410 --> 00:07:33.430
There's a lot of paperwork.

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:35.830
It wouldn't be quick.

00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:37.970
You two are so mean!

00:07:37.970 --> 00:07:39.950
Koikawa-dono didn't it!

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:41.830
Wait, Jinbei-kun!

00:07:42.220 --> 00:07:43.940
We're just a pair of meanies, anyway.

00:07:44.260 --> 00:07:47.980
And why do you suppose 
Shungiku-kun won't tell us?

00:07:53.950 --> 00:07:55.030
<i>Murderer...</i>

00:07:55.030 --> 00:07:57.830
<i>Why are you still alive?</i>

00:08:03.840 --> 00:08:06.270
Is there nothing to drink here?

00:08:07.790 --> 00:08:09.060
Thanks.

00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:14.450
This is great...

00:08:14.450 --> 00:08:16.410
But there aren't any snacks with it.

00:08:16.870 --> 00:08:18.920
Oh! Squid.

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:21.350
Even tentacles... Those go great with sake.

00:08:27.720 --> 00:08:30.170
What are you doing, new kid?

00:08:30.170 --> 00:08:33.150
Getting you out of there, of course!

00:08:33.150 --> 00:08:35.610
Come on, don't be stupid.

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:36.530
They'll catch you, too!

00:08:36.980 --> 00:08:39.010
No, they won't!

00:08:39.010 --> 00:08:43.620
You said you aren't a thief!

00:08:44.840 --> 00:08:49.890
So if I save you and you're innocent,
I won't have done anything wrong.

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:54.010
There's no reason to have you 
jailed in the first place.

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:55.880
How rude!

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:00.220
You really are dumb.

00:09:00.970 --> 00:09:02.520
Give me that.

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:18.450
<i>He cut clean through it with a saw?</i>

00:09:19.300 --> 00:09:22.450
A lot of people have cursed me.

00:09:23.010 --> 00:09:25.250
But I've never met anyone like you.

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:27.250
<b>Kodenma Prison</b>

00:09:25.970 --> 00:09:27.250
What was that noise?

00:09:27.570 --> 00:09:30.020
Trouble! Koikawa's escaped!

00:09:30.020 --> 00:09:31.530
He also took his sword!

00:09:31.530 --> 00:09:32.700
What?

00:09:32.700 --> 00:09:34.010
After him!

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:36.130
What do we do now?

00:09:37.230 --> 00:09:41.980
Obviously, we find the real thief, 
and give him to the magistrates.

00:09:43.070 --> 00:09:47.310
I told them you were innocent, 
but they wouldn't listen.

00:09:47.930 --> 00:09:52.540
And so, I want for them to...

00:09:52.540 --> 00:09:55.570
No, for all of Edo to believe in you.

00:09:55.850 --> 00:09:57.290
As your student...

00:09:57.290 --> 00:10:01.350
I cannot allow my master to 
be suspected of anything.

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:10.580
Koikawa Shungiku's escape
 is my responsibility.

00:10:13.200 --> 00:10:15.250
Koikawa's history?

00:10:15.690 --> 00:10:17.590
I gave it to you long ago...

00:10:19.710 --> 00:10:22.850
I meant absolutely no insult.

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:25.310
You might say

00:10:25.310 --> 00:10:29.060
that he was born to be a murderer.

00:10:27.710 --> 00:10:39.770
<b>Wanted: Koikawa Sanosuke</b>

00:10:29.600 --> 00:10:32.370
Do you remember the gang of thieves

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:37.050
that once operated in Edo: the Black Spiders?

00:10:37.050 --> 00:10:41.330
Their leader was Koikawa Sanosuke, 
and his son was Shungiku.

00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:43.880
<i>You say you can't kill anyone?</i>

00:10:45.540 --> 00:10:48.960
<i>We are the Black Spiders. 
People fear us.</i>

00:10:53.980 --> 00:10:57.990
<i>People won't think much of us 
if our leader's son is such a wimp.</i>

00:11:00.990 --> 00:11:03.540
<i>Shungiku, please don't be upset.</i>

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:04.660
<i>Okiku...</i>

00:11:05.330 --> 00:11:06.640
<i>The reason my son</i>

00:11:07.690 --> 00:11:11.480
<i>can't even kill a man is that you spoil him!</i>

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:16.090
<i>Killing is wrong.</i>

00:11:16.090 --> 00:11:18.300
<i>You must never kill...</i>

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:22.670
His mother, Okiku, was a kind woman, 
far too good for Sanosuke.

00:11:23.510 --> 00:11:26.850
Shungiku must have inherited that trait from her.

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:31.910
He committed many crimes. 
But as his mother had asked,

00:11:32.290 --> 00:11:34.500
he never committed murder.

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:03.180
<i>Shungiku, this isn't—</i>

00:12:03.180 --> 00:12:05.060
<i>Young master, our leader...</i>

00:12:18.700 --> 00:12:21.090
<i>I asked you not to kill, so often...</i>

00:12:21.090 --> 00:12:23.380
That he couldn't fulfill his mother's request,

00:12:23.860 --> 00:12:25.460
followed by his mother's death...

00:12:25.920 --> 00:12:28.050
It drove him mad.

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:30.750
He followed in his father's footsteps,

00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:33.390
killing any who stood in his way.

00:12:34.250 --> 00:12:36.000
Even former companions.

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:38.180
Or magistrates.

00:12:36.880 --> 00:12:46.560
<b>Warrant: Koikawa Shungiku</b>

00:12:38.180 --> 00:12:39.460
Anyone.

00:12:40.070 --> 00:12:42.620
In all, ninety-nine died.

00:12:43.060 --> 00:12:46.370
Thus, he became known as Koikawa Shungiku,

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:48.190
Killer of 99.

00:12:48.650 --> 00:12:49.910
I think we lost them.

00:12:50.270 --> 00:12:51.120
Yeah.

00:12:51.120 --> 00:12:55.790
Where did you learn such 
beautiful swordsmanship?

00:12:56.170 --> 00:12:58.420
That's an odd question to ask right now.

00:13:02.600 --> 00:13:03.720
I don't know.

00:13:04.950 --> 00:13:08.310
I just kept killing, and this is how I ended up.

00:13:08.710 --> 00:13:11.160
Killing? Killing what?

00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:12.010
People...

00:13:13.650 --> 00:13:14.690
Right?

00:13:15.250 --> 00:13:17.440
The Killer of 99, Koikawa Shungiku.

00:13:18.500 --> 00:13:20.940
Yeah, you got that right.

00:13:21.430 --> 00:13:23.280
You stole at Iseya!

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:26.070
And since you've escaped from prison, 
we can kill you here!

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:27.310
It's not like that!

00:13:27.310 --> 00:13:30.020
Koikawa-dono didn't do it!

00:13:30.020 --> 00:13:31.700
Shut up! He's a killer!

00:13:32.190 --> 00:13:36.080
I'll avenge all of my 
companions who you killed!

00:13:40.150 --> 00:13:43.170
The job of arson and theft investigators 
is catching criminals.

00:13:43.910 --> 00:13:45.590
It isn't to kill them!

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:47.180
Shut up!

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:47.800
And get out of the way!

00:14:03.170 --> 00:14:05.860
<b>Oogatana Kamakiri - Bladed Mantis</b>

00:14:06.750 --> 00:14:07.740
It's a bug!

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:18.920
It sliced my sword in two?

00:14:20.900 --> 00:14:23.580
Leave this one to me...

00:14:23.580 --> 00:14:26.760
You work with arson and theft 
to evacuate the civilians.

00:14:27.440 --> 00:14:28.380
Right!

00:14:29.480 --> 00:14:31.100
Let's go, everyone!

00:14:31.400 --> 00:14:32.510
We have no choice.

00:14:33.040 --> 00:14:34.280
Koikawa!

00:14:34.280 --> 00:14:37.480
We'll let you go for now, 
but we'll kill you later!

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:38.720
Forget that!

00:14:38.720 --> 00:14:40.520
We have to get everyone out of here!

00:14:40.970 --> 00:14:43.250
A Bladed Mantis is here!

00:14:43.250 --> 00:14:44.900
Please evacuate!

00:14:45.530 --> 00:14:47.150
Doorman, open the gate!

00:14:49.540 --> 00:14:52.200
I can't run...

00:14:52.560 --> 00:14:55.270
Protecting the people is the 
Insect Magistrate's job.

00:14:57.050 --> 00:14:58.830
Everyone, this way!

00:14:59.930 --> 00:15:01.330
Wait just a second.

00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:12.720
Now that I'm refreshed...

00:15:13.730 --> 00:15:16.520
Life's nothing but a drunken dream.

00:15:16.520 --> 00:15:18.100
And when you wake, you're dead!

00:15:24.680 --> 00:15:26.260
Is that all you have?

00:15:28.600 --> 00:15:30.530
Too easy.

00:15:52.190 --> 00:15:53.470
Show yourself,

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:54.750
Mitsuki.

00:15:56.280 --> 00:15:57.820
So you noticed me, huh?

00:15:57.820 --> 00:15:58.970
You're good, Mugai-kun.

00:16:00.250 --> 00:16:01.820
It's been a long time.

00:16:02.880 --> 00:16:04.130
I came to say hi.

00:16:07.680 --> 00:16:09.130
You're ignoring me?

00:16:09.130 --> 00:16:12.500
It's been so long! Let's talk!

00:16:12.880 --> 00:16:15.940
Hey! Hey! Has anything fun happened in Edo?

00:16:15.940 --> 00:16:17.450
Any good date spots?

00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:19.710
Have you met a nice girl?

00:16:19.710 --> 00:16:21.460
And... And...

00:16:22.320 --> 00:16:26.170
Why did you betray us, the Insect Hunters?

00:16:27.820 --> 00:16:30.110
You're so scary!

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:33.430
But we're finally about to get started.

00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:36.800
Our first target will be a Bladed Mantis.

00:16:37.590 --> 00:16:42.310
So we'd be happy if you'd come back.

00:16:42.880 --> 00:16:44.830
Brother is waiting for you...

00:16:51.830 --> 00:16:53.020
You!

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:56.200
Now we'll just wait for the bug to kill you.

00:17:04.230 --> 00:17:07.790
You can go to hell alone, everyone hating you!

00:17:08.370 --> 00:17:11.340
I have to fight humans before 
I can fight that bug?

00:17:12.110 --> 00:17:16.260
I guess you can't sever karma's bonds.

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:19.720
My hands are stained as black as the swamp.

00:17:20.210 --> 00:17:21.720
All they can do

00:17:22.120 --> 00:17:23.730
is kill!

00:17:35.090 --> 00:17:36.240
Move, kid!

00:17:36.550 --> 00:17:38.450
No, I won't!

00:17:38.840 --> 00:17:41.510
Do you know what he did?

00:17:47.700 --> 00:17:49.710
<i>What's wrong, Dad?</i>

00:17:49.710 --> 00:17:50.960
<i>Scared?</i>

00:17:51.310 --> 00:17:53.870
<i>Sh-Shungiku, hear me out.</i>

00:17:53.870 --> 00:17:54.990
<i>It wasn't me...</i>

00:17:54.990 --> 00:17:57.220
<i>I didn't kill Okiku!</i>

00:18:00.060 --> 00:18:02.390
<i>Your father speaks the truth.</i>

00:18:03.960 --> 00:18:08.150
A group known as the Insect Hunters
 killed your mother.

00:18:09.350 --> 00:18:10.980
<i>The Insect Hunters?</i>

00:18:12.170 --> 00:18:16.390
Due to a mistake, that fool Koikawa 
killed all those people!

00:18:16.390 --> 00:18:18.390
Including my comrades!

00:18:19.780 --> 00:18:22.280
The past is the past, and now is now!

00:18:22.710 --> 00:18:25.040
His swordsmanship does not lie.

00:18:32.430 --> 00:18:34.980
Please take a look at him now.

00:18:35.600 --> 00:18:38.520
His sword protects the people of Edo!

00:18:47.310 --> 00:18:49.270
The other one's yours, new kid.

00:18:49.730 --> 00:18:50.750
Right!

00:18:50.750 --> 00:18:52.060
So is he jelly?

00:18:53.350 --> 00:18:57.360
If a rock is konjac, then is he jelly?

00:18:59.710 --> 00:19:03.210
What you have to ask yourself is 
how much you want to cut it.

00:19:05.600 --> 00:19:07.370
Here I go, bug!

00:19:20.370 --> 00:19:22.970
It's working, Koikawa-dono!

00:19:24.300 --> 00:19:25.470
Just like that!

00:19:25.600 --> 00:19:28.480
<b>Always be ready for a fight.</b>

00:19:25.820 --> 00:19:28.480
Always be ready for a fight!

00:19:31.720 --> 00:19:34.300
<i>Plus Repentance Slash!</i>

00:19:36.350 --> 00:19:38.550
Don't think this atones for anything you did!

00:19:44.840 --> 00:19:46.540
There was money in its stomach?

00:19:47.100 --> 00:19:50.040
Hard to believe a bug was the robber...

00:19:51.710 --> 00:19:52.750
Hey,

00:19:52.750 --> 00:19:56.960
do you want to know why I was there?

00:19:57.320 --> 00:20:03.150
If you couldn't tell them, you must 
have had a very good reason!

00:20:04.350 --> 00:20:06.250
A good reason, huh?

00:20:07.170 --> 00:20:09.050
A-Actually...

00:20:09.050 --> 00:20:10.980
I was attacked by a dog.

00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:15.800
I've never liked dogs.

00:20:16.330 --> 00:20:19.330
One day, I got drunk and 
stepped on a dog's tail.

00:20:20.310 --> 00:20:22.880
So I ran away...

00:20:22.880 --> 00:20:25.980
And I grabbed the first thing I saw.

00:20:25.980 --> 00:20:27.990
It was a dead man's katana.

00:20:28.530 --> 00:20:30.580
The rest is just as you saw it.

00:20:33.360 --> 00:20:37.610
But no one would believe
 a stupid story like that.

00:20:38.130 --> 00:20:42.510
I know if someone had told me that story,
 I'd never have believed it.

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:43.830
I see!

00:20:44.220 --> 00:20:46.350
That must have been terrible...

00:20:47.300 --> 00:20:50.100
<i>He believes me!</i>

00:20:50.700 --> 00:20:53.830
Okay! Let's go get drunk!

00:20:53.830 --> 00:20:54.760
Right!

00:20:59.110 --> 00:21:02.110
You're a good guy, you know that?

00:21:02.110 --> 00:21:03.700
Drink more.

00:21:04.160 --> 00:21:06.490
My stomach's already full, but...

00:21:07.020 --> 00:21:10.850
I couldn't refuse the tea offered by my master.

00:21:15.370 --> 00:21:18.960
I want to be a great samurai like you.

00:21:18.960 --> 00:21:20.130
Samurai?

00:21:20.130 --> 00:21:22.230
I'm just a killer.

00:22:59.980 --> 00:23:02.770
<b>Next Time</b>

00:23:00.550 --> 00:23:02.250
Tenma-dono, I want to learn

00:23:02.250 --> 00:23:03.650
your Full-Power Slap!

00:23:03.650 --> 00:23:05.060
What kind of skill is that?

00:23:05.060 --> 00:23:07.320
<i>Tsukishima-style: Full-Power Slap!</i>

00:23:07.320 --> 00:23:08.070
Grab!

00:23:09.360 --> 00:23:11.170
Next time, on <i>Mushibugyo</i>:

00:23:11.170 --> 00:23:14.000
Ichinotani Tenma, I Can Do It!

00:23:11.570 --> 00:23:14.000
<b>Ichinotani Tenma, I Can Do It!</b>
